Block Lists gathers what a firewall blocks by list into one page:
public address lists (Spamhaus DROP, abuse.ch Feodo Tracker, Emerging
Threats, CINS Army, blocklist.de) fetched daily into aliases, countries
in a GeoIP alias, the DNS block lists of Unbound shown beside them, and
TLS clients cut by their JA4 fingerprint from the Intrusion Detection's
log. The block rules are registered by the plugin and never added to
the owner's own rules. Connections already open to a newly listed
address are cut, and on a Sophos XGS taken out of the coprocessor.

Plugin Changelog
================

1.0.1

* a list chosen again cuts what it names, also what was opened while it was not chosen
* only the aliases Block Lists makes are its own; an owner's alias named blocklists_* is left alone
* the JA4 watch covers the whole minute, so a fingerprint listed mid-minute is cut within seconds
* the IDS log read a line at a time; snapshots written only on a change, by one run at a time
* the rules hook is checked by php -l, before the installer copies it
* removal stops its cuts, deletes its state and empties its tables that nothing uses

1.0.0

* Initial release
